"nethack -X" invokes a non-scoring game in discovery mode;  whereas
"nethack -D" invokes the wizard (or debugging) mode which is also
non-scoring.

But, in order to run the wizard mode, you login-name must match the:

        #define WIZARD_NAME "whoever"

in the config.h file, and this line should be edited before compilation.

And also, as a convention (see above -D -X), I would prefer [ynx?]
better than [ynd?].

